Benchmark Gap: What existing benchmarks do not measure
从evolution中我们可以发现一些现有的static benchmark没有测量的能力吗：
Static agent benchmarks mainly evaluate a model as an agent executor under a fixed harness. 

However, harness-level self-evolution exposes two distinct roles: 
a builder/evolver that writes or updates the harness, and 
a solver/agent that uses the evolved harness. 
Existing evaluations usually collapse these roles into one end-to-end score, so they cannot tell whether self-evolution performance 
comes from the model’s ability to build agents, 
the model’s ability to act as the improved agent, or their interaction.

