Background: LLM agents are increasingly built with harnesses (simple)
This illustrate the background 从而下面能引申到为什么我们要考虑self evolving
LLM agents are no longer just raw models. In real tasks such as software engineering, tool use, terminal operation, and workflow automation, their behavior depends heavily on an external agent harness: prompts, tools, memory, skills, workflow instructions, and environment-specific rules.
Background: Self-evolving agents update the harness from experience 
This discuss the motivation of self evolution: 现有的harness 手工设计不适应快速的deployment time环境变化，所以需要self evolution根据experience update harness
A natural way to make agents improve is to update this harness from execution experience. When an agent fails, receives feedback, or discovers a useful procedure, the resulting lesson can be written back into the harness and reused in future tasks. This gives rise to self-evolving agents: frozen LLM agents whose external harness improves over time without updating model parameters.
Prior work shows harness evolution can improve fixed agents & and limitations of existing methods/benchmarks
现有的work证明了self evolution 这一个scheme的有效性：
Existing works, such as A-Evolve, SkillRL, Reflexion, Self-Refine, GEPA, and Voyager, show that agents can improve by revising prompts, skills, memories, or workflows based on runtime behavior and feedback. 
一些existing benchmarks也同样证明了harness-like artifacts can improve agents: 
SkillsBench shows that curated Skills can substantially improve agent performance, while self-generated Skills often fail to provide the same benefit. PostTrainBench shows how an improvement benchmark can be structured around a bounded autonomous process, strict evaluation constraints, and held-out evaluation. SEA-Eval and Evo-Memory further show that agent evaluation is moving from isolated episodes toward sequential improvement and experience reuse. 
Limitations of existing methods/benchmark -> Why we introduce this benchmark: 
但是他们通常关注的是某一类特定方法的end-to-end效果：However, most of these works ask a single-method, single-agent question: does this update method improve this fixed agent?
但 end-to-end 提升无法解释 source of improvement: This view is useful for showing that a method works, but it does not explain where the improvement comes from. Is the gain driven by the model that turns experience into better harness updates, or by the model that can effectively use the updated harness?
引入self evolution two roles的概念（solver, evolver）：This end-to-end view hides a simple decomposition. A self-evolving agent must do two things. 
First, it must turn experience into a better harness: read failures, feedback, or trajectories and write useful updates. 
Second, it must act with the updated harness: use the revised prompts, skills, memories, or workflows to solve future tasks. These two operations need not require the same foundation-model capability.
