Diagnostic 1: Role bottleneck diagnosis
Question. Is self-evolution more sensitive to the builder or to the solver?

Report.

Spread of builder-marginal gains:

[ \mathrm{spread}_e(\mathrm{BuilderMarginal}(e)) ]

Spread of solver-marginal gains:

[ \mathrm{spread}_s(\mathrm{SolverMarginal}(s)) ]

Interpretation.

Large builder spread: different evolvers vary substantially in harness-update ability.
Large solver spread: different solvers vary substantially in their ability to use evolved harnesses.
Both small: domain, feedback quality, task stream, or budget may dominate.

Take-home. This tells frontier-model labs and system builders whether to invest more in builder-side update generation or solver-side harness utilization.




